<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve"
                        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                        xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                        xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml"
                        xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">

  <!--
    Project-scoped ReSharper severities for the Qodana Community for .NET scan. See
    TotallyHotArcRouter.Qodana.slnx.DotSettings for why these decisions live in .DotSettings files
    rather than in qodana.yaml.

    Short-lived 'HttpClient': the inspection guards against socket exhaustion from churning real
    HttpClients in production. Every one of its 37 findings is in this project, where the client is
    bound to an in-memory TestServer handler and deliberately scoped to a single test so cases cannot
    leak state into each other - there is no socket to exhaust, and sharing one client across tests
    would trade a non-problem for real cross-test coupling.

    Scoped to this project on purpose rather than turned off solution-wide, so a short-lived
    HttpClient in production code is still reported.
  -->
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ShortLivedHttpClient/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

  <!--
    "Fold this into an object or collection initializer."

    All 63 are arrange blocks in this project, and the rewrite makes them worse. A test that reads

        var ledger = new StubLedger();
        ledger.MaxTurnBySession["sess-1"] = 4;   // simulates a restart mid-conversation

    becomes a nested-property initializer with nowhere to put that trailing comment, and the setup
    stops reading as a sequence of arranged facts. Several others would collapse four separate
    DefaultHttpContext.Request assignments into one nested initializer, which is harder to scan and
    harder to diff when a single field changes.

    Scoped to this project rather than turned off solution-wide, so the same finding in production
    code is still reported.
  -->
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=UseObjectOrCollectionInitializer/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

  <!--
    "Merge these checks into one pattern."

    The seven production sites were read individually and four were applied - the genuinely better
    ones, where `is JsonArray { Count: > 0 }` and `is > 0 and <= Ceiling` say what the conjunction
    was spelling out. The seventeen here are assertions and arrange conditions, where merging buys
    nothing: a test's `&&` chain is usually enumerating the conditions it means to check, and a
    merged pattern hides that enumeration.

    This is also what ADR-0008 asks for directly: score smells on production code, because "test
    projects are the regression net, not the catalog". Production stays enabled.
  -->
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=MergeIntoPattern/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
